From 1bb3504fa58d097f0535e94fcf61a44030dab3c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 08:26:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 404/407] SableOS: keyboard test step after keyboard readiness

Adds a Keyboard test step after the keyboard readiness step and before
Wi-Fi. The user types a sentence into one field and seven checks are
ticked as they register: letters, Shift capitals, numbers, Alt
characters, Sym symbols, Space and Backspace. The Q25 has no Fn key, so
there is no Fn check. A modifier key alone shows as pressed; its layer
passes when a character typed with it reaches the field. The field
reports key downs before the IME, so Shift, Alt and Sym register even
when Sable Keyboard consumes them; text from the on-screen keyboard
still passes the checks that need no modifier.

Enter (or the IME's Next action) continues, Skip and Next are always
enabled, and Back/Esc return to the readiness step. If the keys do not
work, the step links to physical keyboard settings (Use on-screen
keyboard) and to Accessibility, each shown only when the screen exists.
The field is focused on entry so the first key types; typed text is not
saved, autofilled, suggested or learned, and only pass states are kept
in memory for the life of the step.

The checks live in the pure SableKeyTest class (IR-014).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FqvfFQhAvko2gkqcxM25Aa
